From 9a275dabe9a9436b4da26fd40e238d5b361c84ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:44:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/14] Fix the custody ABI's consumers: harness registry,
 generated JS ABI

The ABI patch left two consumers broken: the LiteSVM harness's coverage
registry (an exhaustive match over Ix) did not compile, and the JS
client's ABI files generated from frontier-abi/vectors were stale
(sync-web-sdk.mjs --check). The custody instructions are Pending in the
registry (RELEASE_CHECK=1 keeps failing until their LiteSVM tests exist);
the JS files are regenerated by the repository's own script.

Ported to the integration candidate c1e8137e: the harness registry keeps
8's ExtendFrontier beside custody's Pending entries; the generated JS
ABI (gateway client and web sdk) is regenerated by sync-web-sdk.mjs from
the rev-4 vectors (OpenLot is tag 194 = 0xC2). svm-tests compiled with
cargo check --tests only (not run: it generates and signs keys).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C5Nj2cMNVbfXW4D5Pzsbxg
